DocStudioServerTools = Server tools for the PDF editor (optional)
DocStudioServerToolsHelp = Without them, the PDF editor works entirely in the browser. They add the compression of PDF files when saving: Ghostscript first (on the Dolibarr server), Stirling PDF when Ghostscript is not set or fails.
DocStudioGhostscriptPath = Path of Ghostscript
DocStudioGhostscriptPathHelp = gs executable of the Dolibarr server, for example /usr/bin/gs. Empty: no Ghostscript.
DocStudioStirlingUrl = Address of Stirling PDF
DocStudioStirlingUrlHelp = Stirling PDF server reached by the Dolibarr server (not by the browser), for example http://127.0.0.1:8080. Empty: no Stirling PDF.
DocStudioStirlingApiKey = API key of Stirling PDF
DocStudioStirlingApiKeyHelp = If your Stirling PDF server asks for one. Stored encrypted, never shown nor sent to the browser.
DocStudioStirlingApiKeySaved = Key saved (leave empty to keep it)
DocStudioStirlingApiKeyRemove = Remove the key
DocStudioTestTools = Test
DocStudioStirlingOk = Stirling PDF reached, version %s.
DocStudioStirlingKo = Stirling PDF cannot be reached: %s
DocStudioGhostscriptOk = Ghostscript found, version %s.
DocStudioGhostscriptKo = Ghostscript does not answer: %s
DocStudioStirlingBadUrl = Invalid address of Stirling PDF: it must start with http:// or https://.
DocStudioGhostscriptBadPath = Invalid path of Ghostscript: give only the path of the executable, without options.
DocStudioRedactionSetupHelp = Redaction in the PDF editor: every page with a redacted zone is replaced by an image of the page, then DocStudio checks that the hidden text is no longer in the file. On these pages the text can no longer be selected, copied nor found, links and form fields disappear and the file is heavier; the other pages do not change. The new file keeps no metadata, bookmarks, attachments nor previous versions. A rectangle drawn with the Draw tool is not a redaction: any PDF reader can remove it. Replacing the original does not change the copies already sent or filed elsewhere, and an electronic signature of the PDF is lost. Stirling PDF is not used to redact: its zone redaction puts a box over the text without removing it from the file.

